"The first unit of this course described qi as a single pattern of function, but Chinese medicine actually divides it into several named varieties, each tied to a different source and a different job. Source qi, sometimes called original qi, is inherited at birth and stored in the kidney — the closest thing this system has to a starting budget, spent down gradually over a lifetime rather than replenished from scratch. Gathering qi, sometimes called pectoral qi, collects in the chest from what's breathed in and eaten, and powers the heartbeat and the breath directly.": "c45cf0718e92",
